<article class="env-lemma" id="00NT">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00NT">Lemma <span data-tag="00NT">10.106.6</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a regular local ring. Any maximal Cohen-Macaulay module over $R$ is free. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $M$ be a maximal Cohen-Macaulay module over $R$. Let $x \in \mathfrak m$ be part of a regular sequence generating $\mathfrak m$. Then $x$ is a nonzerodivisor on $M$ by Proposition <a href="/tag/00N6" data-tag="00N6">10.103.4</a>, and $M/xM$ is a maximal Cohen-Macaulay module over $R/xR$. By induction on $\dim (R)$ we see that $M/xM$ is free. We win by Lemma <a href="/tag/00NS" data-tag="00NS">10.106.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>